{"type": "root", "attrs": {"type": "node", "context": "cop2", "internal": "lumamatte", "icon": "COP2/lumamatte", "index": "no", "version": null, "namespace": null}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Luma Matte"], "extent": [82, 97]}, {"type": "summary", "indent": 0, "text": ["Sets the alpha to the luminance of the color."], "extent": [97, 151]}, {"type": "warning_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "warning", "indent": 0, "text": ["Old network"], "role": "item", "extent": [16, 38], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["As of Houdini 20.5, use ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/nodes/cop/index", "type": "link", "text": ["Copernicus nodes"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/index.html"}, " instead of Compositing nodes. Though both networks still exist, the Compositing network is now designated as ", {"type": "code", "text": ["COP Network - Old"]}, ". The Compositing network and its nodes will be deprecated and then removed in a future Houdini release."], "extent": [38, 335]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Lumamatte computes the luminance of the color image, and stores it in\nthe alpha matte."], "extent": [194, 282]}, {"type": "note_group", "body": [{"type": "note", "indent": 0, "role": "item", "extent": [282, 288], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["A similar operation can be done with the Channel Copy COP."], "extent": [288, 353]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"level": 1, "id": "parameters", "container": true, "type": "parameters_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [353, 365], "body": [{"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["LumaMatte"], "extent": [365, 386], "body": [{"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Luminance Range"], "extent": [386, 412], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["Allows you t